"Bull. Aust. Math. Soc. 100 (2019), 428–433 (https://www.cambridge.org/core/services/aop-cambridge-core/content/view/86C7F38FE0748BFC2B857A2391185BA4/S0004972719000315a.pdf/div-class-title-on-the-regularity-of-character-degree-graphs-div.pdf)\nciteturn7search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; Tong-Viet showed that his conjecture is true for k = 3 (see [5]). ... Let G be a ﬁnite group and suppose the character degree graph ∆(G) of ... By Theorem 1.2, if ∆(G) is a regular graph with odd order then ∆(G) is complete, ... p = 2 and n = 1 or 6;\n[2]\nRegularity of character degree graphs\n429\nTong-Viet showed that his conjecture is true for k = 3 (see [5]). As the main result\nof this note we prove the following theorem.\nTheorem 1.2. Let G be a ﬁnite group and suppose the character degree graph ∆(G) of\nG has more than two vertices. Then ∆(G) is k-regular for some integer k if and only if\none of the following conditions holds:\n(a)\nk = 0 and G \u001b A5 × C or PSL2(8) × C for an abelian group C; or\n(b)\n∆(G) is a regular bipartite graph and in particular, if k , |ρ(G)| −1, then |ρ(G)|\nis even.\nBy Theorem 1.2, if ∆(G) is a regular graph with odd order then ∆(G) is complete,\nproviding some evidence for Tong-Viet’s conjecture.\nIf ∆(G) is a regular graph\nwith even order, then either ∆(G) is complete (as predicted by Conjecture 1.1), or\nρ(G) = X ∪Y for some disjoint nonempty sets X and Y, such that |X| = |Y| and the\nsubgraphs induced in ∆(G) by X and Y are complete.\nThroughout the paper, all groups are ﬁnite and all characters are complex characters.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRyser's conjecture in the remaining 2-packing cases — MathDB (https://mathdb.com/p/351502/ryser-s-conjecture-in-the-remaining-2-packing-cases)\nciteturn7search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; Ryser's conjecture in the remaining 2-packing cases ... source: Adrián Vázquez Ávila, “A note on extremal intersecting linear